The `candidates` array is deduplicated using `.includes(hit)`, which is O(n) per call (reference equality scan). This loop runs up to 4 times per semantic triple, making anchor resolution O(k²) in the number of candidate hits. For large mechanical triple sets with many shared subjects/objects, this can degrade significantly.

Recommendation: replace the array+includes pattern with a `Set<TypedTriple>` for O(1) membership checks:
```typescript
const candidateSet = new Set<TypedTriple>();
for (const hit of index.bySubject.get(subjNorm) ?? []) candidateSet.add(hit);
for (const hit of index.byObject.get(subjNorm) ?? []) candidateSet.add(hit);
for (const hit of index.bySubject.get(objNorm) ?? []) candidateSet.add(hit);
for (const hit of index.byObject.get(objNorm) ?? []) candidateSet.add(hit);
